      "writtenOn": "2024-04-11T19:50:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As written, this will compose any SkColorFilter on the restore paint into the filter graph that is then evaluated in the layer\u0027s color space. I think this is the behavior we want (and would be consistent with the updated public docs in SaveLayerRec).\n\nBut the alternative could be that while the image filter evaluates in the layer space, the rest of the restore paint operations are in the dst device\u0027s color space (which would require explicitly wrapping the paint\u0027s color filter in a WorkingSpaceColorFilter() if the layer and dst color spaces were different). In either case, I think blending is always going to happen in the dst color space.\n\nWhich way do you lean, @brianosman?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 882,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 882,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "e7c5855159128522eb46599d58faecf649efea32",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
